id: pm-web-yjb2
title: Restore pm-web release pipeline (mistaken runner removal 6691d413)
description: "Regression of pm-web-2xlv (2026-06-09 first restore via PR #7). On 2026-07-06 commit 6691d413 re-deleted .github/workflows and the repo was re-privatized + Actions disabled; npm publishing stalled at 2026.6.14 while commits continued through 2026-07-10. Root cause: author confused pm-web (public self-hosted pm web-UI npm package needing daily releases) with pm-cli-companion (the only repo meant to be private/runner-less)."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: ci,release,release-readiness,security,workflows
created_at: "2026-07-10T15:23:49.763Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-10T15:57:33.286Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-10T15:57:33.285Z"
author: pi-orchestrator
acceptance_criteria: "Secret/PII scan of the private window history (2026-07-05 onward) is CLEAN; .github/workflows/{ci,release}.yml restored from 6691d413^ on a feature branch (not pushed); restored workflows retain fleet-wide fixes (non-main guard, push tag/main after publish, npm-authoritative bun-lag fallback, --ignore-scripts); build, typecheck, tests, audit, pack, changelog:check all green; this pm item logs the scan verdict, restoration, drift, and build/test results."
regression: true
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-10T15:29:34.398Z",codex,"Orchestrator: branch pushed, repo set PUBLIC again (was privatized with the runner removal), Actions re-enabled, PR #25 opened. CI test workflow running; greptile+gemini+coderabbit triggered. After merge: dispatch Daily Release to publish the stalled month of changes (npm still at 2026.6.14)."
close_reason: completed
body: "## Secret/PII scan verdict: CLEAN\n\nScanned every commit since 2026-07-05 (`git log -p --since=2026-07-05`) plus the current tracked tree for: npm/GitHub/Slack/Sentry tokens, DB connection strings, private hostnames/IPs of home infra, non-public emails, .env contents, and `BEGIN ... PRIVATE KEY`.\n\nNo real secrets, private IPs, home-infra hostnames, .env files, or connection-string credentials were found. Findings were all benign/intentional:\n- `stefan@preu.at` + Impressum address (Stefan Preu, Steinbruch 5, 3250 Wieselburg) — public git author email AND legally-required public legal-notice contact (GDPR/Austrian Impressum), not leaked PII.\n- `postgres://user:pass@localhost:5432/pmweb` in README.md, src/db.ts, dist/db.js — clear placeholder/example for the DATABASE_URL env var, not a real credential.\n- `ghp_…` UI placeholder in public/src/views/settings.ts GitHub PAT input — input hint, not a token.\n- `you@example.com` / `colleague@example.com` — example placeholders.\n- False-positive `xox` substring inside an integrity hash in extensions/pm-graph/package-lock.json.\n- The hard-coded dev JWT literal `pm-web-dev-secret-change-in-prod` was already REMOVED by commit 77d1523 (replaced with a generated in-memory dev secret + production JWT_SECRET requirement). src/auth.ts verified clean.\n\n## What was restored\n\n`git checkout 6691d413^ -- .github/` (the targeted parent-checkout approach; a full `git revert --no-commit 6691d413` was attempted first but it also reverted CHANGELOG.md and removed the pm-web-y28b tracking item that 6691d413 legitimately added, so only the workflow files were restored).\n\nFiles restored verbatim from 6691d413^:\n- .github/workflows/ci.yml\n- .github/workflows/release.yml\n\n## Workflow drift vs sibling (pm-todos)\n\nDiffed restored pm-web workflows against /workspace/pm-todos/.github/workflows/. pm-web's restored workflows retain ALL fleet-wide fixes:\n- non-main release guard (\"Check release ref\" step) — present\n- push release tag/main AFTER npm publish — present\n- npm-authoritative bun-lag fallback in bun-verify — present\n- `npm publish --access public --provenance --ignore-scripts` + provenance-less fallback — present\n\nDrift is intentional pm-web-specific or cosmetic (kept pm-web's own versions, nothing broken):\n- release.yml cron `41 3` (pm-web) vs `23 3` (pm-todos) — staggered schedule, intentional.\n- release.yml: pm-web uses npm scripts (`npm run changelog:full`/`changelog:check`/`release:notes`) and an inline `node -e` version-bump for manifest.json + src/index.ts; pm-todos calls `npx pm-changelog` directly with a hardcoded pm-todos item-url-base and `npm run release:update-version`. pm-web's pattern is correct for this repo.\n- release.yml commit paths: pm-web commits `src/index.ts` + \"Release pm-web ...\"; pm-todos commits `dist`/`src`/`index.ts` conditionally + \"Release ${repo} ...\". pm-web-specific.\n- release.yml GitHub release title \"pm-web ...\" vs `${{ github.event.repository.name }}`. pm-web-specific.\n- ci.yml: cosmetic only (`pull_request: {}` vs `pull_request:`; step label \"package graph\" vs \"package dependencies\").\n\n## Build/test results (branch fix/restore-release-pipeline-and-public-visibility)\n\n- npm ci: 182 packages, 0 vulnerabilities, clean.\n- npm run typecheck (graph+server+frontend): PASS.\n- npm run build (graph+server+frontend): PASS.\n- npm test: 48/48 tests PASS, 0 fail (no Postgres needed — legal-routes tests use an in-memory createApp).\n- npm audit --omit=dev: 0 vulnerabilities (direct). NOTE: the `npm run audit:prod` wrapper exits non-zero locally due to a project-scoped `--allow-scripts` policy quirk; the underlying audit is clean.\n- npm run pack:dry-run: 196 files, 2.1 MB, ok.\n- npm run changelog:check: \"Changelog is up to date\".\n\n## Branch\n\n`fix/restore-release-pipeline-and-public-visibility` off main (commit 931c889). NOT pushed. Repo visibility / GitHub Actions re-enablement handled by the orchestrator (no repo settings changed here).\n\n## Related\n- Supersedes/re-fixes the 2026-07-06 regression introduced by 6691d413 (pm item pm-web-y28b, which closed by deleting the workflows + disabling Actions — the mistaken action this item reverses).\n- Regression of pm-web-2xlv (2026-06-09 first restore via PR #7), which was the same class of fix for the earlier no-runner misapplication."
